{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7EXEWYA353osuJuvtuW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Before I draft, a few questions. The answers would change what the email says:\n\n1. **Who gets this email, and have the 14 already heard?** Is it going to all staff, or only the people at Maple Street and Route 9? Will those 14 have been told in person before it goes out? Learning about your own branch closing from a company-wide email lands very differently from getting it as a follow-up.\n\n2. **What actually gets better, and for whom?** The 14 are trading a 9-to-5 schedule for rotating shifts that can run until 8 p.m. Unless the email names concrete gains, many of them will read \"better\" as spin. Gains could include higher pay for some, working from home, training or a career path, or no longer facing slow, empty branches. What would you point to? For the other five branches, is there a real gain to name, like fewer transferred calls or shorter waits for their members?\n\n3. **Where is the center, and when does it open?** Will people commute somewhere new? Does training start before March 31?\n\n4. **What's the decision process?** When do staff have to accept the new role or take severance? Will each person get a one-on-one meeting? How does \"same pay or higher\" get set for each person?\n\n5. **Where do people take questions?** Is there a named HR contact, a staff meeting, or an FAQ?\n\nIf you don't know some of these yet, say so. I'll leave those parts out rather than guess."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":442,"cache_read_input_tokens":9577,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":442},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use